// "Amass <subtype> N" with its reminder text [CR#701.47a]: "If you don't
// control an Army, create a 0/0 black <subtype> Army creature token. Choose
// an Army you control. Put N +1/+1 counters on it. It's a <subtype> in
// addition to its other types." Lean `amass`.
//
// STOP (updated by `semantics-v2-macro-param-kinds`): the amassed subtype
// is spliced into a `Vec<Subtype>` position (the token's own subtypes,
// twice), which no `String` value can fill — it needs a `Subtype`-typed
// param. `deckmaste_semantics_v2::ron::param_types()` now has one (this
// ticket's crate fix), but `deckmaste_construction_core::macro_def::
// ParameterType` — the SAME closed eight-name enum, mirrored independently
// on the english_v2/typed side that reads every `plugins_v2` declaration's
// `params:` field too (`docs/decisions/semantics-v2.md` §11: neither crate
// depends on the other for the shared declaration file, so BOTH readers
// must accept a param type before any declaration can use it) — has no
// `Subtype` variant and was out of this ticket's authorized file scope
// (`crates/deckmaste_semantics_v2/src/{ron.rs,reader.rs}` and its tests,
// plus the xtask drift test, per the dispatching brief). A one-sided fix is
// unusable: `both_readers_accept_every_builtin_declaration` fails on
// `UnknownParameterType { name: "Subtype" }` from the construction_core
// side alone. Left bodyless pending that companion fix.
KeywordAction(
    name: "Amass",
    spelling: "amass",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "amass",
        third_person: "amasses",
        frame_set: Custom(frames: [[ObjectNounPhrase, Amount]]),
    ),
)
